{"id": "unknown-2026-08-26-001", "date": "2026-08-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "A joint Japan-Taiwan research project to develop circularly-polarized OLED technologies", "content": "<p>A group of five Universities from Japan and Taiwan have launched a joint project to develop core technologies for circularly-polarized OLEDs (<a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/bright-side-brannan-circularly-polarised-oleds-why-are-researchers-so\">CP-OLED</a>). These kind of OLEDs natively emit circularly polarized light, enabling higher-performance devices, and are of high interest to the research community (<a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/bright-side-brannan-circularly-polarised-oleds-wh", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/joint-japan-taiwan-research-project-develop-circularly-polarized-oled", "type": "rss"}]}
